ptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcbaechinger/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcbaechinger/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcbaechinger/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcbaechinger/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/916269596","html_url":"https://github.com/google/ExoPlayer/issues/9257#issuecomment-916269596","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/9257","id":916269596,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAT2ozs42nSoc","user":{"login":"christosts","id":54315740,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MzE1NzQw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54315740?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/christosts","html_url":"https://github.com/christosts","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christosts/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christosts/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christosts/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christosts/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christosts/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christosts/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christosts/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christosts/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christosts/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-09-09T16:51:58Z","updated_at":"2021-09-09T16:51:58Z","body":"Thanks for filing the issue with details. Before we add a check in the code, I'd like to understand more of the context under which you observe this error. I cannot see a straightforward path for the PlaybackStatsListener to reach that state, and there may be another bug hidden somewhere in there. \r\n\r\nHave you managed to reproduce locally? Or, do you have any indications under what use-case this error occurs (from any kind of logging you may be collecting)? Also, do you add the PlaybackStatsListener on the player right after creating the player or later?\r\n\r\nContext for the last question: For `guessMediaTimeBasedOnElapsedRealtime()` to throw:\r\n1. `mediaTimeHistory` must be empty\r\n2.  the PlaybackStatsListener must be in PLAYBACK_STATE_PLAYING\r\n3.  the `mediaTimeMs` passed in `maybeUpdateMediaTimeHistory ` must be C.TIME_UNSET ([link to 2.14.0 version](https://github.com/google/ExoPlayer/blob/r2.14.0/library/core/src/main/java/com/google/android/exoplayer2/analytics/PlaybackStatsListener.java#L244)).\r\n\r\nI wasn't able to figure out a straightforward path for this happen. For example, 1 & 2 can be achieved if you add the PlaybackStatsListener on an already playing player. Yet, deciding that an event does not belong to a session could happen between item transitions, but still the PlaybackStatsListener handles such cases. \r\n\r\nIf you have more data on what context this error occurs, it would help us fix a potentially trickier bug.\r\n\r\nThanks","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/916269596/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"christosts","id":54315740,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MzE1NzQw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54315740?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/christosts","html_url":"https://github.com/christosts","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christosts/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christosts/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christosts/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.githu