ub.com/users/greyski/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/greyski/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/greyski/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-09-09T17:39:54Z","updated_at":"2021-09-09T17:39:54Z","body":"(from the same team as @shashachu)\r\n\r\n> Have you managed to reproduce locally?\r\n\r\nWe have not been able to reproduce locally and have set `keepHistory` to `false` for all our instances of `PlaybackStatsListener` since reporting to resolve the issue. e.g. `PlaybackStatsListener(false, null)`\r\n\r\n> Or, do you have any indications under what use-case this error occurs (from any kind of logging you may be collecting)?\r\n\r\nFrom our breadcrumbs we see 2 things:\r\n\r\n- 1 or more videos may be playing on-screen at once\r\n- 2 or more instances of ExoPlayer may be present in memory\r\n\r\n> Also, do you add the PlaybackStatsListener on the player right after creating the player or later?\r\n\r\nWe attach the `PlaybackStatsListener` in our overridden `VideoView.setPlayer(player: Player?)` method like so:\r\n```\r\n    override fun setPlayer(player: Player?) {\r\n        val oldPlayer = (getPlayer() as? SimpleExoPlayer)\r\n        playbackStatsListener.run {\r\n            oldPlayer?.removeAnalyticsListener(this)\r\n        }\r\n        super.setPlayer(player)\r\n        playbackStatsListener.run {\r\n            newPlayer?.addAnalyticsListener(this)\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n```\r\nBut to answer your question: _Usually_ right after creating an `ExoPlayer` instance, but _sometimes_ later as we keep a cache of already instantiated `ExoPlayer`s for re-use.\r\n\r\nIn theory, we shouldn't be adding this listener to an already playing instance of `ExoPlayer` as our playback callbacks happen _after_ `setPlayer` is called, and the players we cache have already called `stop()` prior to entering the said-cache.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"htt